1
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:11,480
A school buys 25 calculators at 7 dollars 96 each.

2
00:00:11,530 --> 00:00:14,980
The office has no calculator to hand!

3
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:19,250
How could you work out the total quickly, in your head?

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,670
What is 25 times 7 dollars 96?

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,650
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,740
7.96 is 4 cents less than 8.

7
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:31,270
25 times 8 is 200.

8
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:36,790
But each calculator is 0.04 less, and there are 25 of them.

9
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,570
25 times 0.04 is 1.

10
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:43,800
So the total is 200 minus 1, which is 199 dollars.

11
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:49,060
Remember: 9 times 4.2 is 10 times 4.2, minus one 4.2.

12
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:53,180
That is 42 minus 4.2, which is 37.8.

13
00:00:53,230 --> 00:00:55,960
And look for pairs that make 1.

14
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:58,130
0.25 times 4 is 1.

15
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:01,930
Here are some ways to make decimal calculations easier.

16
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:05,180
Round and adjust, like the calculators.

17
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:06,330
Use factors.

18
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:15,450
15 is 3 times 5, so 3.6 times 15 is 3.6 times 3, which is 10.8, then times 5, which is 54.

19
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,780
Use fractions.

20
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:24,050
0.25 is a quarter, so 0.25 times 7.2 is 7.2 divided by 4, which is 1.8.

21
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:25,730
And look for pairs.

22
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:27,780
0.2 times 5 is 1.

23
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:28,590
Your turn.

24
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,090
Work out 0.2 times 4.6 times 5.

25
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:34,670
Pause the video and try it.

26
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,370
Pair 0.2 with 5.

27
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:38,170
0.2 times 5 is 1.

28
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:41,170
And 1 times 4.6 is 4.6.

29
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:42,480
Here is the method.

30
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:47,640
Step 1: look for numbers close to a whole number or a round number.

31
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:53,390
Step 2: look for pairs that multiply to make 1, 10 or 100.

32
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,750
Step 3: split a number into factors, or use fractions.

33
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:02,250
0.25 is a quarter, 0.5 is a half, 0.2 is a fifth.

34
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:07,610
Step 4: follow the order of operations, and check with an estimate.

35
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:11,460
Work out 3.6 times 8.5, plus 3.6 times 1.5.

36
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:18,290
Both parts have 3.6, so take it out: 3.6 times, bracket, 8.5 plus 1.5.

37
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,690
8.5 plus 1.5 is 10.

38
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:23,640
3.6 times 10 is 36.

39
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:25,880
Work out 5.2 divided by 0.5.

40
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:30,120
0.5 is a half, and there are 2 halves in every whole.

41
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:34,760
So dividing by 0.5 is the same as multiplying by 2.

42
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:35,530
Your turn.

43
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:38,480
Finish it: what is 5.2 divided by 0.5?

44
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:41,590
Pause and work it out.

45
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:44,550
5.2 times 2 is 10.4.

46
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:49,490
In the same way, dividing by 0.25 is multiplying by 4.

47
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:54,890
So 6.3 divided by 0.25 is 6.3 times 4, which is 25.2.

48
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:58,420
Work out 0.125 times 7.3 times 8.

49
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:02,910
0.125 is an eighth, so 0.125 times 8 is 1.

50
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:05,920
And 1 times 7.3 is 7.3.

51
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:08,310
Dan works out 15 times 5.98.

52
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:11,250
Which line goes wrong first?

53
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:12,740
Line 2 is wrong.

54
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:17,580
There are 15 lots of 0.02 to subtract, not just one.

55
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:20,080
15 times 0.02 is 0.3.

56
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:23,340
90 minus 0.3 is 89.7.

57
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:29,610
Shops often set prices like 4 dollars 99, because they look smaller than 5 dollars.

58
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,730
Round and adjust beats that trick.

59
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:38,890
6 items at 4 dollars 99 cost 6 times 5, which is 30, minus 6 cents.

60
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:41,470
That is 29 dollars 94.

61
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,900
One last question.

62
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:44,640
Work out 7.3 times 99.

63
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:48,190
Pause the video and answer.

64
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:50,920
99 is 1 less than 100.

65
00:03:50,970 --> 00:03:53,530
7.3 times 100 is 730.

66
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:59,170
Subtract one 7.3: 730 minus 7.3 is 722.7.

67
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,270
To remember: round and adjust.

68
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:05,030
Adjust by the difference times the multiplier.

69
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:09,840
Use factors, and pairs that make 1, 10 or 100.

70
00:04:09,890 --> 00:04:17,870
Remember: 0.25 is a quarter, 0.5 is a half, 0.2 is a fifth, and 0.125 is an eighth.

71
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:22,130
Use the distributive law, and the order of operations.

72
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:27,310
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.4 on Camday.
